    "created_at": "2016-04-26T14:41:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-26T14:41:05Z",
    "body": "Per offthread discussions with @bzbarsky I need to make it clearer that \"relevant\" is a predicate that applies to objects, in contrast to current/incumbent/entry which are ambient values. That is, you can have \"relevant settings object of X\" and \"relevant settings object of Y\". In most algorithms it's \"the relevant settings object of **this**\" that matters.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
